158" :question/problem "Let $c=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $d=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].$ Find $c+d.$" :question/worked-solution "We add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c+d & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2-3 \\\\ 0+2 \\\\ -1+5 \\\\ 4+7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-34158/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab0d2c2f-e7a4-51bb-a20a-f28c2f7ded8b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-34158"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-34223"] :question/problem "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$ Find $3a+2b.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply each component of $a$ by $3$ and each component of $b$ by $2.$ Then, we add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+2b & =3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9-6 \\\\ 6-4 \\\\ 15+2 \\\\ 3+10 \\\\ -6+12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 17 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-34226/selection/3a5592ce4ca794890159791f44cd838a1ce319de9cfaf057f7d7509e607b28c3" :answer/id #uuid "c1b58d3b-8588-50ef-9d09-322d0de135b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:an