in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}l\\cdot m & =3 \\\\ 5\\cdot 1+x\\cdot x+2\\cdot 4+x\\cdot (-1)+2x\\cdot (-3) & =3 \\\\ 5+{x}^{2}+8-x-6x & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2}-7x+13 & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2}-7x+10 & =0 \\\\ (x-5)(x-2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe get two solutions, ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2}=2.$ Since we need $x>3$, our final answer is $x=5$ only." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-73949/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "94f8e0e5-8d8a-516a-8f46-d76e94305df4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73949"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-34169/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "52400ada-8177-5139-a7fb-1e126270104c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34169/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "4ee18bbc-16d2-5e9e-a0c3-dedbf1e2965d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34169/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "6775c1b9-346e-5040-ac5e-d90057fbf9ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34169/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "80905519-a9f8-55e7-b111-362478b6c8ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34169/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "b7a2f5c3-060b-5a73-a1c1-954d9a33e0d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34169/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b8fc8f13-33ca-5124-8bbb-11949a16315f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-34169/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-34169/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-34169/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-34169/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-34169/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-34169/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-34169" :question/id #uuid "b473e158-894c-5e8f-9a39-9a3f46be7f95" :question/math-academy-id "q-34169" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{4} \\\\ 4 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{-2} \\\\ -8x \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ If $u\\cdot v=12$ and $x<6$, find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Starting from the equation $u\\cdot v=12,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =12 \\\\ 2{x}^{4}\\cdot 2{x}^{-2}+4\\cdot (-8x)+12\\cdot 4+6\\cdot 2 & =12 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-32x+48+12 & =12 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-32x+48 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-8x+12 & =0 \\\\ (x-2)(x-6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe get two solutions, ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=6.$ Since we need $x<6$, our final answer is $x=2$ only." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-34169/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "94f8e0e5-8d8a-516a-8f46-d76e94305df4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-34169"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105110/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "3553b9ed-8bc4-581a-8bbd-893215a9ee29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105110/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "3a37d95b-af0f-5033-95a0-34db41d8cb34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105110/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "af48bc56-a6d6-59b4-8ec9-de84230c3367" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105110/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "47b981d4-ee99-56d8-982e-79b7e21382e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105110/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "a8e44d2d-ed07-5a7f-9939-69bb167432d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105110/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b84b2e70-d118-5a43-b272-6382b997fbba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105110/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-105110/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-105110/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-105110/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-105110/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-105110/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105110" :question/id #uuid "64634ee1-b105-533f-8237-440ecbf93930" :question/math-academy-id "q-105110" :question/problem "Let\n$p=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ y-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $q=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].$\nIf $p\\cdot q=0$, find the value of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "Starting from the equation $p\\cdot q=0,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $y$ and then solve for $y$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ 9\\cdot 0+(y-3)\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-4)+4\\cdot y & =0 \\\\ y-3-12+4y & =0 \\\\ 5y & =15 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105110/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "94f8e0e5-8d8a-516a-8f46-d76e94305df4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105110"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4782"] :question/problem "Let $[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ Find $\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathbf{a}.$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each component of $\\mathbf{a}$ by $\\dfrac{1}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}a & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4783"] :question/problem "Let $[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]$ Find $\\dfrac{1}{3}\\mathbf{a}+\\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply each component of $\\mathbf{a}$ by $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ and each component of $\\mathbf{b}$ by $\\dfrac{1}{2}.$ Then, we add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}a+\\frac{1}{2}b & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1-2 \\\\ 2-3 \\\\ 4+1 \\\\ -3-4 \\\\ 1+5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4784"] :question/problem "If $[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ then what is $\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 3+3\\cdot (-4)+(-5)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =2+12-12-30 \\\\  & =-28\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4785"] :question/problem "Let be $[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ x \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ x \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ If $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=0,$ find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Starting from the equation $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}=0,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 10\\cdot x+x\\cdot x+0\\cdot 8+5\\cdot 5 & =0 \\\\ 10x+{x}^{2}+25 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+10x+25 & =0 \\\\ (x+5)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $x=-5.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
